 "![Curve IV](images/1d/1d45e88e15b95a0aa156c9ce28c20e07366f556a7d0fcd39dd8a369b384fc783.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8658a678-c6ba-5ca2-b63b-0885c74173b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97928" :question/problem "Which of the following curves is simple, closed, and negatively oriented?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented.\n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the curves:\n\n- Curve I is negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\n- Curve II is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve III is not negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed counterclockwise, so it is positively oriented.\n\n- Curve IV is negatively oriented. The arrows indicate that the curve is traversed clockwise.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is curves I and IV only" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048655 :topic/id #uuid "b2c456e2-ef0a-5a75-95da-68bb5f61da4a" :topic/math-academy-id 3356 :topic/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves"} :activity/title "Simple, Closed, and Oriented Curves" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418052} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418068}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172669 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uu