ty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72da8c2e-5747-5cf0-addd-5e327ef519dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-98036" :question/problem "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains two holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is regions I and III only"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091 :topic/id #uuid "d9b41e19-22fc-5fad-93ae-b8f50010d70b" :topic/math-academy-id 3557 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3b87e3a-d17f-5d16-a9ee-8bdda6d42f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439603} {:answer/id #uuid "87018b61-01ec-510f-8fd1-7d6db056af27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3b87e3a-d17f-5d16-a9ee-8bdda6d42f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439603} :answer-field/id #uuid "d542c682-d8b5-5051-a7cb-60f1509b7b1e" :answer-field/key "The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d64fb74-88cb-53a7-a06c-3b70bb7f6274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439605} {:answer/id #uuid "bec31bb0-4e5d-511d-afd5-742b83de0357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bec31bb0-4e5d-511d-afd5-742b83de0357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439606} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87c1b9b-fab1-5cdf-bb7d-886d867b3796" :answer-field/key "The function is zero at $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f33342a6-71e7-55a1-88ba-63522644016c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439607} {:answer/id #uuid "b683d925-eb8f-5ed2-85c9-33a9d51ed2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f33342a6-71e7-55a1-88ba-63522644016c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439607} :answer-field/id #uuid "02f59618-0384-53ab-a17c-8912c7664860" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $[- π, π]$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440161}] :question/id #uuid "3291f5a6-141c-577f-9e01-4f06e16f89ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-27015" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Cosine attains its maxima at x=2n*pi, vanishes at x=3pi/2, and has range [-1,1]. Only statement “The function is zero at $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091 :topic/id #uuid "d9b41e19-22fc-5fad-93ae-b8f50010d70b" :topic/math-academy-id 3557 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68a428aa-620c-537b-bed4-6525636bfc6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439609} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bdaabe-318f-5a44-a993-5dc144a01cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2bdaabe-318f-5a44-a993-5dc144a01cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439610} :answer-field/id #uuid "c19eff62-0f3d-5e8b-8840-f4fa3fa30937" :answer-field/key "The zeros of the function are $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e122d41-3d05-51c1-8ec6-c73fbca7dcd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439611} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab71ce6-dc10-5b55-86c4-8863ebadb312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e122d41-3d05-51c1-8ec6-c73fbca7dcd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439611} :answer-field/id #uuid "12845eb8-7a86-57fa-a87d-28447fbed3a1" :answer-field/key "The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{3π}{2} + 2nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440163} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c69287cc-e1d6-5913-b9fc-cfeb0e6876ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439613} {:answer/id #uuid "433b23fc-2e50-5918-ad8e-38d59e8d6077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c69287cc-e1d6-5913-b9fc-cfeb0e6876ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439613} :answer-field/id #uuid "a99ea223-df14-549f-8f0a-56f14ff03cc4" :answer-field/key "The range of $y = \\cos x$ is $[- 1, 0]$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440164}] :question/id #uuid "4431905d-f46d-548a-987b-b6164fd2cc5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-27021" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Cosine has zeros at x=pi/2+n*pi. At x=3pi/2+2n*pi it is zero, not maximal, and its range is [-1,1]. Only “The zeros of the function are $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050523 :topic/id #uuid "5049bff8-1875-5713-9a67-c3aa9836de2c" :topic/math-academy-id 3558 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba1a255-23c5-558c-890e-352eda666203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438028} {:answer/id #uuid "81040fec-7087-5a36-951b-b14d732d3182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ba1a255-23c5-558c-890e-352eda666203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438028} :answer-field/id #uuid "d005fdab-8b78-5385-b8aa-903a81e93357" :answer-field/key "The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb0045bc-f2f1-542d-bb18-f3e3a32d2249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438030} {:answer/id #uuid "72151a10-5577-5c23-b443-f401e6df03cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72151a10-5577-5c23-b443-f401e6df03cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438031} :answer-field/id #uuid "b788b23d-3122-5950-affc-e24e292331da" :answer-field/key "The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f160f821-e2d0-550e-97fc-505a5402176a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438032} {:answer/id #uuid "6d124318-fd4c-51c0-8d63-f26f3899820c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f160f821-e2d0-550e-97fc-505a5402176a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438032} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba780c82-a764-5e2e-ac73-af96e4c3fadd" :answer-field/key "The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac898e3a-bbc1-536e-8415-2d3fbc798e28" :question/math-academy-id "q-27638" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$” is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement “The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$” is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement “The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050523 :topic/id #uuid "5049bff8-1875-5713-9a67-c3aa9836de2c" :topic/math-academy-id 3558 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06caa996-019d-55b8-9b18-5c983270de02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439615} {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2f5e64-32f3-5522-8385-0836cdf1b1de" :answer-field/key "The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0e3f19-9827-5a02-9335-759832aa58f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439617} {:answer/id #uuid "25bf5a5c-a822-56a1-a1c2-c6a5ab56d691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c0e3f19-9827-5a02-9335-759832aa58f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439617} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a3ab15-7920-5551-b932-d3776cb36d30" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $y ∈ (-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2})$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a5ad809-5893-5399-b9f3-ad07e3a9d1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439619} {:answer/id #uuid "1518fe23-d68e-51c4-ba9d-5901e8279447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a5ad809-5893-5399-b9f3-ad07e3a9d1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439619} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ce653d-94c4-5b5c-8d40-d92ea9bebea4" :answer-field/key "The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440167}] :question/id #uuid "95d49fd8-cd30-53eb-a4a3-b8a8c0494e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-27660" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Tangent has vertical asymptotes at pi/2+n*pi and range all real numbers. Its domain excludes pi/2+n*pi, rather than n*pi. Only “The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec8c126b-beb0-5259-95a8-ee03317b9dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477289} {:answer/id #uuid "05b4a708-dd67-557a-9e5d-3cec0dfaf56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec8c126b-beb0-5259-95a8-ee03317b9dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477289} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9fdd20-93bb-54d2-8f45-dd434f374b95" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(T)=1$,  where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ca155e7-6b82-5264-aff3-a5b9bbf22322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477291} {:answer/id #uuid "d241b648-c419-53a1-bd11-5a4510ba9eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ca155e7-6b82-5264-aff3-a5b9bbf22322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477291} :answer-field/id #uuid "8474779a-6aa5-57d6-8c8a-638b08fec6e2" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Im}(T)$ contains no vectors of ${R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85d7e293-6acb-57a3-84e4-89d7e0daf5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477293} {:answer/id #uuid "c9be56df-604d-5bf1-b89a-a5381de8206d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9be56df-604d-5bf1-b89a-a5381de8206d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477294} :answer-field/id #uuid "6637f2a2-acef-52c2-99ff-897ed538dbfe" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4acbb26f-7e4b-53ce-a37d-bd74763516c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38297" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\text{rank}(T)=1$,  where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$” is false. In our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “$\\text{Im}(T)$ contains no vectors of ${R}^{2}$” is false. The image of $T$ contains the vector zero vector $0=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$ is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/id #uuid "1c611a71-aaa1-5a41-a6cd-aa83bbba97af" :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"} :activity/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553853} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554744}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049991 :topic/id #uuid "245d7b8c-ac58-53e1-bbb6-af3096067f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3567 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosecant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c5e2592-4591-5762-bcbe-2782ea0f3180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439767} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc8ccba-ce7d-5e48-8754-9ea49736590b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bc8ccba-ce7d-5e48-8754-9ea49736590b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439768} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f557e4-66ef-5920-8da5-88cce596386c" :answer-field/key "The point $(π,-1)$ is not on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6880fb21-3096-58cb-af07-7d1e2ea7dd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439769} {:answer/id #uuid "0cd10553-ba3f-56b6-ad32-275f9052a89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cd10553-ba3f-56b6-ad32-275f9052a89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439770} :answer-field/id #uuid "49359634-c5ac-52d1-a03b-87b9054fe601" :answer-field/key "The function has a vertical asymptotes at $x = nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eb04900-1fcb-52ce-91bc-e54e340f3cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439771} {:answer/id #uuid "b8452449-f7ba-5c1c-9d12-c1bb509ee50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8452449-f7ba-5c1c-9d12-c1bb509ee50c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439772} :answer-field/id #uuid "058bbf0f-d4f4-55ca-8a1f-a84af0d4303a" :answer-field/key "The value $y = 2$ is in the range of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440243}] :question/id #uuid "5961bc49-07f6-5191-b949-28358553d498" :question/math-academy-id "q-42912" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Cosecant is undefined at pi and at every n*pi, so (pi,-1) is not on its graph and those x-values are vertical asymptotes. It takes the value 2 where sin(x)=1/2."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176493 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85473916-efab-54cc-8019-f73b8d004fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460029} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d633f9-241d-5408-96ab-be6f460d75e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85473916-efab-54cc-8019-f73b8d004fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460029} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7eaa29b-e3b2-519f-8493-c9b4b97a14b2" :answer-field/key "$(0,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e34f1a82-723e-5044-9c8b-05394e7c8cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460031} {:answer/id #uuid "1d0e6fa2-164b-5d06-89b9-9523a9fbab04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e34f1a82-723e-5044-9c8b-05394e7c8cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460031} :answer-field/id #uuid "12e615de-f408-5827-885a-3812da8f4683" :answer-field/key "$[0,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ffe3706-e794-5508-a886-5b2a3a0e2663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460033} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9a827e-456d-56a4-b4a7-8fe36d4f7beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb9a827e-456d-56a4-b4a7-8fe36d4f7beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460034} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8337631-8ee5-5459-b864-8dd85e062eb9" :answer-field/key "$[1,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9ff6e93-5783-568e-aaac-4c58f2e3a7ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-47779" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-1, & x<0.5 \\\\ 4-{x}^{2}, & x\\ge 0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- The interval $(0,1)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- Now, consider $[0,2].$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0.5}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0.5}(x-1)=(0.5)-1=-0.5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0.5}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0.5}(4-{x}^{2})=4-(0.5)^{2}=3.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=0.5$ are not the same. Hence, $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=0.5.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[0,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, consider $[1,2].$ The only discontinuity of the function $f(x)$ is at $x=0.5,$ which is not in the interval $[1,2].$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is continuous on the interval $[1,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[1,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205c5518-c67a-5784-8cc7-55b42ce7fb0e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether the Extreme Value Theorem Is Applicable to a Function Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65c1bc06-df71-54fe-afe7-b360d01c06b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460035} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f152d9-063b-5c1d-8b75-3bfec9b74ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65c1bc06-df71-54fe-afe7-b360d01c06b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460035} :answer-field/id #uuid "02b0c099-5bf0-521a-92ba-61b7010f80e8" :answer-field/key "$[-1,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e9191d6-529b-5bdb-aff4-2652ae2c3f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460037} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeebf75-da3d-501f-8c76-f1319acdf861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9191d6-529b-5bdb-aff4-2652ae2c3f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460037} :answer-field/id #uuid "8afdd8c3-8c39-559c-8274-02958ad373a3" :answer-field/key "$(1,3]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4152dea0-399a-54a0-b2bf-c11251ba3440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460039} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c60cd4-bd45-5f5f-bf57-dee7650bb566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5c60cd4-bd45-5f5f-bf57-dee7650bb566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460040} :answer-field/id #uuid "56a6a813-2828-5871-a539-dddbc5064efb" :answer-field/key "$[-4,-1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6825513-42a8-5d50-a0d6-c0c31a89a69f" :question/math-academy-id "q-47780" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2ae902b1cccc00b59401ecba306ef7f6f47e92f6439614c13c349283d9e763ff.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,2]$ is closed, but the function is not defined at $x=2.$ So, it can't be continuous at this point. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,3]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-4,-1]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-4,-1].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-4,-1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fd58e8-aaed-556d-888a-e6413102b169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460041} {:answer/id #uuid "81922915-68b9-5c54-8bee-784c6d39c2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6fd58e8-aaed-556d-888a-e6413102b169" :answer/type {:db/id