db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ee96606-8ba8-569e-8f90-21918ad24c63" :question/math-academy-id "q-47787" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={log}_{2}⁡x?$ \n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $(0,5]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,5]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,5].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,5]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on $[0,5]$ because this interval contains points where the function is not defined. In particular, it is not defined at $x=0.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[1,5]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80f70124-c2af-5ee2-b010-11aa7285d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460047} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1a1354-5046-5b4b-9996-9e9aa5387d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80f70124-c2af-5ee2-b010-11aa7285d0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460047} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6caf9b-4980-529e-97b4-de8f4825f3e5" :answer-field/key "$[0,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bfa2956-3ca2-54c2-95f5-1587e0995009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460049} {:answer/id #uuid "9c0dc7bf-2fa2-5fd5-bc3c-554429a21d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bfa2956-3ca2-54c2-95f5-1587e0995009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460049} :answer-field/id #uuid "08d86bc0-031b-56ef-9be7-e1e3067eb03e" :answer-field/key "$(1,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf06108a-57f4-54ba-a053-e5138c94a590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460051} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f7b59e-3df8-5891-bd78-1c7831303d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf06108a-57f4-54ba-a053-e5138c94a590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460051} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3ce31e-0b4e-56e4-9147-5055ff5d8219" :answer-field/key "$[-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76bcbf01-0552-53da-87ac-24d7932ac118" :question/math-academy-id "q-47922" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}^{2}+1, & x<1 \\\\ -x+2, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals.\n\n- Consider $[0,2].$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}({x}^{2}+1)=(1)^{2}+1=2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}(-x+2)=-1+2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the limits from the left and from the right of $x=1$ are not the same. Hence, $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=1.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[0,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- Finally, consider $[-2,2].$ The only discontinuity of the function $f(x)$ is at $x=1,$ which is belongs to the interval $[-2,2].$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[-2,2],$ and the extreme value theorem is not applicable on this interval.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048837 :topic/id #uuid "c4d057b8-12ac-5f2a-94f7-d0b239050514" :topic/math-academy-id 3560 :topic/title "Radius of Convergence of Power Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7f35540-d877-5eff-9e46-9439bd28ec69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460095} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4c483d-ffe3-5e86-98b6-c03e4155d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f4c483d-ffe3-5e86-98b6-c03e4155d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460096} :answer-field/id #uuid "9841c9db-718a-5217-a9a9-2021b0db1a98" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6953953-6666-5aa6-8f5a-31b6d8b9b9c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460097} {:answer/id #uuid "d30127ba-908a-527d-aa7a-042d852768d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6953953-6666-5aa6-8f5a-31b6d8b9b9c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460097} :answer-field/id #uuid "abb6d5fd-b93b-5453-845d-8ee19992b512" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460915} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f478b29b-1cb6-5d73-9f17-d0dfc143c08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460099} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4cfc9d-8dfe-5742-b10a-7fc9139893bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f478b29b-1cb6-5d73-9f17-d0dfc143c08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460099} :answer-field/id #uuid "aad46ace-a494-50f8-bcf6-8a332bbdc665" :answer-field/key "The series diverges at $x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e682c29-6698-5a0f-9318-fe5823633b7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-50878" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{3}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{3}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,2).$\n\n![](images/03/03901ede0b4fadb59556c63aa4534b3a9e20c1e8188388e6256434ece03d9211.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=0$” is true. Since $0\\in [-1,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$” is false. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement “The series diverges at $x=2$” is false. Since $2\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The series converges at $x=0$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049991 :topic/id #uuid "245d7b8c-ac58-53e1-bbb6-af3096067f47" :topic/math-academy-id 3567 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cosecant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aadfbfd-7e0d-5462-9403-7ec6f34bcd45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439867} {:answer/id #uuid "36512727-2b25-560b-a5ef-a6a4dca23d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36512727-2b25-560b-a5ef-a6a4dca23d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439868} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14982a7-98ac-5534-aa55-8a5040b1aa77" :answer-field/key "The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3081db96-8e26-52e9-95d2-ce823865c78c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439869} {:answer/id #uuid "0f14ba72-6dd9-5b85-8fb4-3a959179e0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3081db96-8e26-52e9-95d2-ce823865c78c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439869} :answer-field/id #uuid "632309ee-0c98-5584-910d-0b95c24c4b57" :answer-field/key "The function has a zero at $x = \\frac{π}{2}$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b38f072-608f-59e8-ac23-79a3eeb7fa91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439871} {:answer/id #uuid "db27e3a1-ed43-5079-8562-a73f366e243b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db27e3a1-ed43-5079-8562-a73f366e243b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439872} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2616ba-1558-574f-a2d0-2541e9af7773" :answer-field/key "The function takes the value $-1$ at $x =-\\frac{π}{2} + 2nπ$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440293}] :question/id #uuid "82d5c89d-6391-5689-957e-6be71174a415" :question/math-academy-id "q-65310" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Cosecant is defined exactly when x is not n*pi, never equals zero, and equals -1 at -pi/2+2n*pi."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049035 :topic/id #uuid "d53c1458-9af5-589b-8d7b-d3dbe4e7a946" :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c4e27d3-28a4-5c4c-b64c-c97318703993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477127} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f8030c-9e32-5ae9-ba46-541f78c07d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c4e27d3-28a4-5c4c-b64c-c97318703993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477127} :answer-field/id #uuid "4325ea6f-c825-59af-b418-4d03cd726cfe" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477533} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3faf9aed-2e42-5804-8239-bab232db5dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477129} {:answer/id #uuid "79b9715e-0243-5db8-8f75-37135a50d142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79b9715e-0243-5db8-8f75-37135a50d142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477130} :answer-field/id #uuid "a37b91e8-5472-5172-b3e5-dd6ac76e24fa" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4b88ba-409e-5305-8634-f9e216ca2a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477131} {:answer/id #uuid "39a4163f-abdc-5a7d-aba6-6ba3d2a8afc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b4b88ba-409e-5305-8634-f9e216ca2a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477131} :answer-field/id #uuid "22b592d7-5a89-5dcf-83da-ad19a65e44f0" :answer-field/key "The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44bbbc90-f4f2-5074-bbff-3d0cc0edc535" :question/math-academy-id "q-124004" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}v-u \\\\ u+v-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-u+v \\\\ u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-2$ is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1=-2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $det(A)=-2$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 9" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440905} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440936}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179770 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e39ae7fc-ff0a-5b97-8e13-1f15b12a07e5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Invertible Affine Transformations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048492 :topic/id #uuid "a459a1e3-e019-5c4e-a702-5c6685ca3dec" :topic/math-academy-id 3707 :topic/title "The Inverse of an Affine Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfe983a6-86f9-5e85-b458-f781e21c140d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448110} {:answer/id #uuid "0a98043d-5dff-5ea4-9e03-3d50d77054b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe983a6-86f9-5e85-b458-f781e21c140d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448110} :answer-field/id #uuid "41004b63-e782-515c-b8db-25e0f62efb36" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449095} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb4ef7fd-13ca-58f5-a761-f38a0e1a271e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448112} {:answer/id #uuid "800c874a-5daf-5173-b771-501d14f8edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ef7fd-13ca-58f5-a761-f38a0e1a271e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448112} :answer-field/id #uuid "d532ade3-90d1-5f1e-9570-f9069f48be56" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449096} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a595b56c-93c8-5082-873d-5f72788d8c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448114} {:answer/id #uuid "02c905a9-96d8-56f3-b13d-9f2cb1327c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02c905a9-96d8-56f3-b13d-9f2cb1327c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448115} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9bbb31-cd77-53c4-9780-2f910cb04323" :answer-field/key "The transformation is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "267c4ee8-beb7-545b-be5a-57b42fce6778" :question/math-academy-id "q-124111" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-v,\\,y=u+2v+1.\n$$\n\nSuppose that $A$ is the matrix that represents the linear transformation associated with $T.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is false. The given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ u+2v+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}u-v \\\\ u+2v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=0$ is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1=3\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation is invertible” is true. Since $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the affine transformation is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The transformation is invertible” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049035 :topic/id #uuid "d53c1458-9af5-589b-8d7b-d3dbe4e7a946" :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f120e747-ca95-5759-b8ec-eafc3a35ba62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448122} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c25924-cf5c-5a7d-8af6-0e25982699fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f120e747-ca95-5759-b8ec-eafc3a35ba62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448122} :answer-field/id #uuid "693e9f5c-89c9-56bd-af7c-801e081bcba7" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f54989c-7784-5627-8e6b-6f62adbd34df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448124} {:answer/id #uuid "9d55e342-05bd-5933-9261-faa213e3ffa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f54989c-7784-5627-8e6b-6f62adbd34df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448124} :answer-field/id #uuid "34483a14-9440-50e5-bdd6-6b571ee1fd6c" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "714d09d4-f329-541c-9d1f-ea0d6c330506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448126} {:answer/id #uuid "a8422e70-f2b5-5477-bb06-828103e9ac69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8422e70-f2b5-5477-bb06-828103e9ac69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448127} :answer-field/id #uuid "492621a3-4f38-5cae-b371-5b8ae037e9ba" :answer-field/key "The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91a59d9f-f2b5-5450-b850-f776f534f3f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-124199" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=3u-v+2,\\,y=v-u.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v+2 \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Statement $det(A)=-2$ is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049035 :topic/id #uuid "d53c1458-9af5-589b-8d7b-d3dbe4e7a946" :topic/math-academy-id 3706 :topic/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation"} :activity/title "The Image of an Affine Transformation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435512} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435516}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} {:answer/id #uuid "9682a02a-0b80-592c-b204-2e00e64c9de0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459473} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8082197-4ec5-5193-873e-90d47f00746b" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fbca2-a092-5b1e-95d7-018e7d1f5edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459475} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459476} :answer-field/id #uuid "422cd737-9b8c-53f2-a0cd-c12e1ad7286c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbcc0ff-2235-56bb-aa08-904c6e3a229b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459477} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459478} :answer-field/id #uuid "07711a4e-3e3f-5c90-b74e-ec28eded9fbf" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d69dfd-31b1-5851-b7cd-9ea022ec672e" :question/math-academy-id "q-125380" :question/problem "![](images/14/145b9dcc1e52dec65d64245afa89fba77e0d0cda5a919b52009e2397f3f03e16.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/20/20121d30445c9e756f1c2c024713bc6cd6f0464cfcfc24df68bc30c766c4988e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/0f/0ff98536c275458d68deabda91f56bf63e7c8f59f5ea79c68292332d8cd58d4f.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$; ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4b12aa-dfc8-5cf6-bb46-fa30cda83363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459479} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebe448c-6d78-52eb-b87a-c0f6378a526d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a5163-4335-5da1-a308-4afc6fa83343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459481} {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6785c8-4fa8-5419-98ef-b6ca891fd2fe" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7f457e-5e87-5921-9c97-354280faa2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459483} {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459484} :answer-field/id #uuid "5480c90b-6e84-5672-a102-83d8323aaae1" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26c0cce0-6deb-59c6-a9c4-06e4698080d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125381" :question/problem "![](images/50/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false while statement ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/34/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$; ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049147 :topic/id #uuid "de74c316-f607-5e04-8847-2af8b65a611b" :topic/math-academy-id 3694 :topic/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions"} :activity/title "Interpreting Line Integrals of Vector-Valued Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550361} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551387}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd85d8b-be1b-575e-80ac-713251f2e060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a2d901-52dc-580c-b53b-e7be3980d2fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459485} :answer-field/id #uuid "68a91996-588b-523d-920f-19a0c8f2360d" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c0216-e1b1-5dd3-8feb-cc822c3d9a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459487} {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e40de4-f646-5021-9351-81097f6cd6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459488} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5092c7-0f51-5842-8bc5-c41ed85755e5" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} {:answer/id #uuid "872e5857-37ec-5931-83c9-83ec8a9ea82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a377412f-eec0-5aeb-b5a0-47d4b28ce15c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459489} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe9a2195-fa09-5aad-adbc-06b68d958d2b" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d320327-1d15-55df-b5dd-771fb0fd1831" :question/math-academy-id "q-125394" :question/problem "![](images/27/270e72ebedac3741e1b7086021b16dc0975ae9852d402673c8044a67f8f774fb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $E$ and the vector field $F,$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $E$ is traversed once in the **clockwise** direction. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe now recall the following:\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$ is false, while statement ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves clockwise along $C.$ \n\n![](images/db/dbb6dbdfabccf7a94c67781210238c647e6f3a2e428cb79c4debdbff5e124720.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement ${∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves counterclockwise along $C.$\n\n![](images/1c/1c5aa77b0a89e1fcb0782c9d969d3a81bbec47b004f07bd3a53ccd10e623ba6e.png)\n\nSo, $Γ={∮}_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179740 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f30993e-b5c7-5d8a-9b27-2aed2c9223e1" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Sign of a Circulation From a Diagram" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050773 :topic/id #uuid "659072cc-8b2c-5e8d-b6a6-88321581f47f" :topic/math-academy-id 3713 :topic/title "Circulation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8b6878-85b8-58eb-a242-cf54f14a0ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459491} {:answer/id #uuid "31fb75c7-